  "solution": {
    "text": "Parabolas <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> touche each other at line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;<br />(<math><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> both parabola are inverse of each other)<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> is a common tangent at <math><mi>P</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> we get point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> by solving <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> point of contact <math><mi>P</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> equation of normal at <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math>",
